WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.990
Meet the fennec fox, a
fox of the hot desert.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.360
Its ears are enormous.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.580
Blood vessels near their
surface radiate heat.

4
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.160
It rarely drinks.

5
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.680
Most of its water comes from its food.

6
00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:17.840
And it is active at night,
sheltering in a burrow by day.

7
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:22.250
So how did the fennec fox end
up so well suited to the desert?

8
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.560
In this mission, you'll pin down
exactly what counts as an adaptation,

9
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:27.890
and what doesn't.

10
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.160
Then you'll put that idea to
work on other living things,

11
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.550
such as grasses that grow
where most plants cannot.

12
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.470
Your mission: explain how the fennec
fox came to suit the desert so well.
